{
  "question_id": "naming.ensemble.original-counted-map-prefix-construction",
  "question": "Does original namespace ensemble create/configure preserve a counted raw-NUL String map-prefix head when namespace-qualifying and reading back the map, independently from later command lookup, in the actual C8.4\u20139.1 and current initialized Jim providers?",
  "problem_statement": "The map prefix is constructed by a counted object append; using command publication extent during construction can drop a NUL suffix from the stored and publicly queried map before lookup. Create and configure select different entered namespaces, and rooted heads avoid qualification independently.",
  "channel": "A registered original C/Jim callback is invoked in an actual entered namespace by fixed ASCII namespace eval source. The callback constructs head with Tcl_NewStringObj/Jim_NewStringObj from explicit raw bytes and length, constructs original prefix and map list objects, and invokes the actual namespace ensemble create/configure vector without parsing or serialising the map. Readback query and subsequent public invocation are distinct original vectors. Each provider/case is a fresh fullInit process; no binary NUL construction or ByteArray substitutes the original String.",
  "probe_sha256": "a54fbcb61246d7ab55944af90578043c8a42f9af0e85c5b700fdc30b42aadd76",
  "cases": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "id": "create-relative-raw-nul"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "id": "create-rooted-raw-nul"
